      {
        "type": "note",
        "title": "D210 vs D225 vs D230S1",
        "content": "Tapo D210 vs D225 vs D230S1 \u2014 Key Differences (Short Table)\n\nQuick Takeaways\n\nD210 \u2014 Best budget choice\n- Cheapest\n- Battery only\n- No hub\n- Basic features\n\nD225 \u2014 Best flexibility\n- Can run wired or battery\n- 180\u00b0 head\u2011to\u2011toe view\n- Strong AI detection\n- Great middle\u2011ground option\n\nD230S1 \u2014 Best overall\n- Highest image quality\n- Spotlight + color night vision\n- PIR sensor reduces false alerts\n- Comes with hub for better reliability\n\n###############################\n\nTapo D210 vs D225 vs D230S1 \u2014 Key Differences (Short Table)\n\nFeature | Tapo D210 | Tapo D225 | Tapo D230S1\nPower | Battery only (6400 mAh) | Battery or Wired (dual\u2011power) | Battery only (6700 mAh)\nResolution | 2K 3MP | 2K QHD (4MP) | 2K 5MP\nField of View | 160\u00b0 diagonal | 180\u00b0 diagonal (head\u2011to\u2011toe) | 170.6\u00b0 H / 140.1\u00b0 V\nNight Vision | IR only | IR (no spotlight listed) | Color night vision with spotlight\nChime / Hub | No hub required | No hub required | Hub included (acts as chime)\nLocal Storage | microSD up to 512GB | microSD up to 512GB | microSD up to 512GB\nAI Detection | Basic motion detection | People / packages / vehicles (AI) | Advanced AI (with PIR sensor)\nBattery Swap | No (built\u2011in) | Yes (battery pack) | Yes (battery pack)\nBest For | Simple, budget setup | Flexible install (wired or battery) | Best image quality + spotlight + hub reliability\n"
      }
    ]
  },
